v3-5 ec-fe i18n + dark/light theme: done
date: 2026-09-19 (completed after FE-CONVENTION lock + user [lang]-file correction)
app: examples/ecommerce-app-fe (MONOREPO: apps/landing + apps/shop + shared types/)

sharing: single source in types/ - i18n/{config,routing,request,navigation}.ts, theme/{theme-context,DisplayControls}.tsx,
  messages/{en,vi}.json. Both apps' next.config wrap createNextIntlPlugin("../../types/i18n/request.ts");
  both tsconfigs map @shared/* -> ../../types/*; globals.css @source covers types/. No duplicated dictionaries.
  Chosen over per-app copies because one dictionary and one request config is the only shape that cannot drift.

locales: ["en","vi"], default "en", cookie "northwind-locale" (1y), timeZone "Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh".
routing: [lang] segment inside each app's router root + src/middleware.ts createMiddleware(routing) both apps.
deps: next-intl@4.14.4 (exact pin; Next 15.5.25-compatible; published 2025-09-11).

structure (FE-CONVENTION locked): route slots are thin shells - page.tsx `const Page = () => <XPage />`,
  layout.tsx `Layout`. Pages live at components/pages/<X>Page/{index,component,classNames}: index is the
  connected half (server async: fetch*/getTranslations/getLocale/SHOP_URL/ROUTES; derives xxxStateOf),
  component.tsx is the pure `XBase` twin taking exactly {state, props, on}. Chrome lives at
  components/layouts/<X>Layout/ taking ONLY {content: ReactNode}; index resolves copy+locale hrefs+theme,
  base takes {state, props, on, body: ComponentType} (academy's PublicProfileLayout shape).
  SHOP_URL is server-only (fs projection) so it crosses into the client tree via
  apps/landing/src/modules/shop-url.tsx (ShopUrlProvider/useShopUrl) beside messages in AppProviders.

theme: shared custom provider (types/theme/theme-context) - light/dark/system, localStorage "theme",
  paints .light/.dark + color-scheme on documentElement, follows prefers-color-scheme in system mode;
  GrammarRoot theme={resolvedTheme ?? "system"} flips data-grammar-theme on the same answer.
  Toggle: shared DisplayControls (theme + locale switch) mounted in both layout chromes.

strings: 71 leaf keys per locale, full en/vi parity (ICU {count} plural + {url}/{reason}/{name}/{email}/{id}
  interpolations). Includes order-status labels; Vietnamese only inside types/messages/*.json.
routes moved: landing / -> /[lang]; shop / -> /[lang] (redirects to /{lang}/browse), browse, cart, checkout,
  account. Internal hrefs read modules/routes ROUTES + `/${locale}` prefix; usePathname from shared
  i18n/navigation keeps isCurrent comparisons locale-free.

verify: npx eslint apps types -> 0 errors | npm run typecheck (tsc --noEmit) -> 0 |
  npm run build -> landing /[lang] + 45.9kB middleware, shop /[lang]{,/browse,/cart,/checkout,/account}
  + 46.3kB middleware, all dynamic, EXIT:0.
per-rule: pre-marker sweep was 984 errors -> eslint --fix fixed 944 mechanical (indent/quotes/semi) ->
  40 structural hand-fixed via the twin restructure (public-component-signature x8, no-inline-class-name x24,
  require-export-jsdoc x8) -> 0 remaining. Route-slot names verified by v3-3 (route-slot-fixed-name).
blockers: none. Note: 2 npm audit advisories reported by the next-intl install were left un-fixed
  (audit fix would touch unrelated deps). Build emits next-intl webpack cache-parse warnings + a
  multi-lockfile workspace-root warning - both pre-existing/benign, neither fails the build.
